Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:51:37 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Optional OpenMP parallelisation of the cost function

`make OPENMP=1` builds ROHSA with OpenMP; the default build is unchanged
(the directives are comments to a compiler without -fopenmp).

Parallel loops, all over independent sky columns:
- the model/residual/objective loop of f_g_cube_fast (one spectrum per
  pixel, objective as a reduction);
- the gradient/regularisation loop for each Gaussian (each pixel writes
  only its own derivatives; the per-Gaussian sums are reductions);
- the zeroing of deriv;
- convolution_2D_mirror.

No large array is copied per thread: the private variables are scalars
and one spectrum-sized model array. With OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 the result is
bit-for-bit the same as the serial build; with more threads the sums are
grouped differently and results differ only by rounding.

